# Executive Dashboard — Savings Pots & Round-Ups
## Stakeholder Briefing · MMP · Document Status: Reviewing

---

## At a Glance

| | |
|---|---|
| **Feature** | Savings Pots & Round-Ups |
| **Phase** | MMP — building on a shipped MVP |
| **Status** | Reviewing |
| **Owner** | Product |
| **Doc Version** | 0.3 |

---

## The Job We're Solving

> **Customers want to put money aside steadily for a future life event without turning saving into another chore.**

Today they patch this together with manual transfers, spreadsheets, and separate savings accounts — all with weak progress visibility and no connection to the moments when money actually moves (salary arrivals, card purchases).

The MVP proved customers will create and use named pots. The MMP question is: **will they keep making progress once the novelty fades?**

---

## What This Stage Adds

| Capability | Why now |
|---|---|
| **Recurring contributions** (weekly / monthly) | Removes dependence on memory — the core step from MVP to habit loop |
| **Card round-ups** | Connects saving to daily spending moments automatically |
| **Pause / stop controls** | Trust requires customers to always feel in control of automatic money movement |
| **Failure notifications** | Automation that fails silently erodes trust faster than no automation at all |
| **Progress visibility** | Balance + target + contribution history on every pot |
| **Contextual entry points** | Salary deposit moments and card settings surface the feature where intent is already high |

---

## What's Out of Scope (Intentionally)

| Out of Scope | Rationale |
|---|---|
| Interest-bearing savings products | Different regulatory structure; not needed to prove the habit loop |
| Shared or family pots | Adds permissions and social UX that don't test the core behavior |
| Funding from external accounts | Staying inside the app keeps trust and complexity manageable |
| Investment-linked goals | Separate product stream, separate job |

---

## Entry Points

```
Savings Hub (app home)   →  Default intent entry
After salary deposit     →  Customers are deciding what to do with money
Card settings            →  Customers thinking about spending are primed for round-ups
```

---

## P0 Requirements Summary

**Automated Funding**
- AF.1 · Recurring contributions on weekly and monthly cadences
- AF.2 · Card round-ups from eligible posted transactions
- AF.3 · Pause or disable without closing the pot
- AF.4 · Failure notifications with explanations

**Controls & Transparency**
- CT.1 · Clear explanation of round-up mechanics (timing, refunds, transfers)
- CT.2 · Available balance display with explanation of pot fund status
- CT.4 · Withdrawal to current account with clear spendability timing

**Progress Visibility**
- PM.1 · Balance, target progress, and latest contribution visible from pots overview

---

## Success Metrics & Targets (12-week window)

| Metric | Target | Why it matters |
|---|---|---|
| Consecutive progress rate | **>40%** of activated customers contribute in two consecutive months | Core proof the product builds durable saving habits |
| Funded goal activation rate | **>18%** of eligible customers create or use a funded pot | Confirms MMP is reaching beyond existing heavy users |
| Automation adoption rate | **>35%** of activated customers enable recurring contributions or round-ups | Validates the new features are solving a real need |
| Contribution success rate | **>95%** of attempted contributions complete | Reliability floor — automation that fails breaks trust |
| Withdrawal confusion contacts | No material increase vs. baseline | Guardrail against accidental trust erosion |

---

## Gate to MLP Investment

| Condition | Timeframe |
|---|---|
| Consecutive progress improves materially, automation adoption is healthy, and trust-related contact rates remain stable | Within 12 weeks of launch |

---

## Key Assumptions Being Tested

| # | Assumption | Threshold |
|---|---|---|
| A1 | Customers with automation enabled contribute more consistently than manual-only users | Automated cohort ≥1.5× more likely to contribute in two consecutive months |
| A2 | Salary and card-settings entry points outperform savings-hub-only entry | Contextual entry points ≥20% higher activation |

---

## Risk Radar

| Risk | Mitigation |
|---|---|
| Round-up calculation errors on refunds / reversals | Explicit handling rules required in card transaction event feed |
| Balance display inconsistency creating confusion | Ledger and balance services must reflect completed transfers accurately |
| Notification fatigue reducing opt-in | Nudges configurable and bounded in frequency |
| Automation feeling opaque | Every automated movement paired with a clear, jargon-free explanation |

---

## Systems That Must Be Ready

- Current-account ledger & balance services
- Internal transfer service (recurring + round-ups + withdrawals + pause/stop)
- Card transaction event feed (posted transactions only)
- Refund and reconciliation rules
- Notification infrastructure

